$ =========================================================================
$ cessna210_strip.bdf — Cessna 210 Centurion-like GA aircraft with DECOUPLED
$ STRIP BODY PANELS (VLM aero model + strip-theory fuselage representation).
$
$ Strip variant of cessna210_body.bdf.  The fuselage is represented by two crossing
$ DECOUPLED STRIP body panels instead of cruciform VLM panels:
$   * horizontal strip body panel (CAERO1 400, XY plane, normal +Z) — body lift/pitch;
$   * vertical   strip body panel (CAERO1 500, XZ plane, normal +Y) — body sideforce/yaw.
$ Their CAERO1 PID points to a PSTRIP (not a PAERO1), so each box is an independent
$ 2-D section with its OWN ΔCp-vs-α curve and NO horseshoe vortex, NO wake, and NO AIC
$ coupling to any other box (see sbeam.aero.strip).  Consequences vs the cruciform:
$   * the strip body CANNOT contaminate the wing/HTP/VTP — its block of the influence
$     operator is diagonal, so the lifting-surface loads are unchanged no matter where
$     the strip sits (overlap is harmless; there is no WT2-ratio conditioning to watch);
$   * it carries NO interference/fence effect either (a decoupled element is transparent
$     to the wing's flow) — it is a pure load device tuned to the total-airplane targets.
$ The body correction (sbeam.aero.body_correction.build_strip_body_correction) sets each
$ box's slope (STRIPK) and local Δα (W2GJ) so the TOTAL airplane Cm/Cn/Cl match the CFD/WT
$ "TOTAL" row of sample/cessna210_body_section_data.csv.
$
$ Coordinate system: X = freestream (forward), Y = starboard, Z = up; origin at nose.
$ Units: SI (m, N, kg, Pa).  Full-span model (SYMXZ=0).
$
$ Splining: the body panels carry SPLINE0 (zero-displacement) — they inject no load into
$ the fuselage beam (a tuning load, not a real airload), exactly as the cruciform deck.
$ =========================================================================
$
SOL 101
$
SUBCASE 1
  TITLE = Cessna 210 1g Static (structure only; aero via Aero tab / SOL 144)
  SPC   = 1
  LOAD  = 10
  DISPLACEMENT = ALL
  SPCFORCE     = ALL
$
BEGIN BULK
$
$ ----------------------------------------------------------------- MATERIAL
$ Aluminium alloy (2024-T3 representative): E=70 GPa, G=26.9 GPa, nu=0.3, rho=2700
MAT1, 1, 7.0e10, 2.69e10, 0.3, 2700.0
$
$ ---------------------------------------------------------------- PROPERTIES
$ PID 1 — fuselage equivalent beam   A=0.020, I1=0.010, I2=0.010, J=0.015
PBAR, 1, 1, 0.020, 0.010, 0.010, 0.015
$ PID 2 — wing spar box              A=0.004, I1=8.0e-4 (flap), I2=8.0e-5 (chord), J=3.0e-4
PBAR, 2, 1, 0.004, 8.0e-4, 8.0e-5, 3.0e-4
$ PID 3 — empennage box (HTP/VTP)    A=0.002, I1=2.0e-4, I2=2.0e-5, J=1.0e-4
PBAR, 3, 1, 0.002, 2.0e-4, 2.0e-5, 1.0e-4
$
$ --------------------------------------------------------------------- NODES
$ Fuselage spine (y=0, z=0.6 cabin centreline)
GRID, 1, , 0.50, 0.0, 0.60
GRID, 2, , 2.70, 0.0, 0.60
GRID, 3, , 5.00, 0.0, 0.60
GRID, 4, , 6.90, 0.0, 0.60
GRID, 5, , 8.00, 0.0, 0.60
$
$ Wing elastic axis (~40% chord, z with 1.5 deg dihedral) — root then stbd/port
GRID, 10, , 2.70, 0.0,  1.250
GRID, 11, , 2.655, 2.80, 1.323
GRID, 12, , 2.610, 5.60, 1.397
GRID, 111, , 2.655, -2.80, 1.323
GRID, 112, , 2.610, -5.60, 1.397
$
$ HTP elastic axis (z=0.70)
GRID, 20, , 7.32, 0.0,   0.70
GRID, 21, , 7.36, 0.865, 0.70
GRID, 22, , 7.40, 1.73,  0.70
GRID, 121, , 7.36, -0.865, 0.70
GRID, 122, , 7.40, -1.73,  0.70
$
$ VTP elastic axis (vertical) — root extended down to z=0.60 (intersects HTP plane)
GRID, 30, , 7.20, 0.0, 0.60
GRID, 31, , 7.36, 0.0, 1.45
GRID, 32, , 7.525, 0.0, 2.30
$
$ ------------------------------------------------------------------ ELEMENTS
$ Fuselage CBARs (along X) — orientation vec (0,1,0)
CBAR, 1, 1, 1, 2, 0.0, 1.0, 0.0
CBAR, 2, 1, 2, 3, 0.0, 1.0, 0.0
CBAR, 3, 1, 3, 4, 0.0, 1.0, 0.0
CBAR, 4, 1, 4, 5, 0.0, 1.0, 0.0
$ Wing root strut (fuselage up to wing EA) — orientation vec (1,0,0)
CBAR, 5, 2, 2, 10, 1.0, 0.0, 0.0
$ Wing CBARs (along Y) — orientation vec (1,0,0)
CBAR, 11, 2, 10, 11, 1.0, 0.0, 0.0
CBAR, 12, 2, 11, 12, 1.0, 0.0, 0.0
CBAR, 111, 2, 10, 111, 1.0, 0.0, 0.0
CBAR, 112, 2, 111, 112, 1.0, 0.0, 0.0
$ Tail struts (fuselage to HTP / VTP roots) — orientation vec (0,1,0)
CBAR, 6, 3, 4, 20, 0.0, 1.0, 0.0
CBAR, 7, 3, 4, 30, 0.0, 1.0, 0.0
$ HTP CBARs (along Y) — orientation vec (1,0,0)
CBAR, 21, 3, 20, 21, 1.0, 0.0, 0.0
CBAR, 22, 3, 21, 22, 1.0, 0.0, 0.0
CBAR, 121, 3, 20, 121, 1.0, 0.0, 0.0
CBAR, 122, 3, 121, 122, 1.0, 0.0, 0.0
$ VTP CBARs (along Z) — orientation vec (0,1,0)
CBAR, 31, 3, 30, 31, 0.0, 1.0, 0.0
CBAR, 32, 3, 31, 32, 0.0, 1.0, 0.0
$
$ --------------------------------------------------------------- CONSTRAINTS
$ Fix all 6 DOFs at the nose reference node (ground/wind-tunnel mount)
SPC1, 1, 123456, 1
$
$ --------------------------------------------------------------------- LOADS
$ 1g body acceleration, -Z
GRAV, 10, 0, 9.81, 0.0, 0.0, -1.0
$
$ ============================================================== AERODYNAMICS
$ Reference geometry (full-span): CREF = wing MAC, BREF = wing span, SREF = wing area.
$ Moments are reported about the origin (RCSID 0).  Field 8 (sbeam extension) is the
$ default Mach for Prandtl-Glauert (0 = incompressible).
AEROS, 0, 0, 1.471, 11.20, 16.24, 0, 0, 0.0
$
$ Aerodynamic panel property for the FLYING surfaces (ordinary VLM, Phase A stub)
PAERO1, 10
$
$ Strip body-panel property: marks CAERO1 400/500 as DECOUPLED strip bodies.  The
$ optional field 3 is the nominal per-box lift-curve slope dΔCp/dα_local; left blank it
$ defaults to π — half the 2π flat-plate value ("50% normal surface").
PSTRIP, 20
$
$ Chordwise NCHORD = 6 (>=2 required for the section-moment correction; >=4
$ recommended for converged pitching moment). Spanwise NSPAN sized for box AR ~1.
$
$ ---- Wing starboard: 16 x 6 = 96 boxes
CAERO1, 100, 10, 0, 16, 6, 0, 0, 1
+, 2.00, 0.0, 1.250, 1.75, 2.15, 5.60, 1.397, 1.15
$ ---- Wing port: 16 x 6 = 96 boxes
CAERO1, 150, 10, 0, 16, 6, 0, 0, 1
+, 2.00, 0.0, 1.250, 1.75, 2.15, -5.60, 1.397, 1.15
$
$ ---- HTP starboard: 8 x 6 = 48 boxes
CAERO1, 200, 10, 0, 8, 6, 0, 0, 1
+, 6.90, 0.0, 0.70, 1.05, 7.10, 1.73, 0.70, 0.75
$ ---- HTP port: 8 x 6 = 48 boxes
CAERO1, 250, 10, 0, 8, 6, 0, 0, 1
+, 6.90, 0.0, 0.70, 1.05, 7.10, -1.73, 0.70, 0.75
$
$ ---- VTP (single surface, "span" is Z): 6 x 6 = 36 boxes
$ Root extended down to z=0.60 so the fin crosses the HTP plane (z=0.70).
CAERO1, 300, 10, 0, 6, 6, 0, 0, 1
+, 6.60, 0.0, 0.60, 1.50, 7.10, 0.0, 2.30, 0.85
$
$ -------------------------------------------------- DECOUPLED STRIP BODY PANELS
$ Two crossing strip surfaces standing in for the fuselage.  PID 20 → PSTRIP, so these
$ are DECOUPLED strips: each box loads only on its own local α/β, with no coupling to
$ the lifting surfaces.  Because a strip cannot contaminate, the placement is chosen for
$ PHYSICAL interpretability (spanning the fuselage so the moment arms are realistic) —
$ NOT to avoid the empennage; an overlap here would change the wing/tail loads by exactly
$ zero.  Tuned by build_strip_body_correction to the CFD/WT "TOTAL" targets.
$
$ ---- Horizontal strip body panel (XY plane at z=0.30, normal +Z): 2 x 8 = 16 boxes
CAERO1, 400, 20, 0, 2, 8, 0, 0, 1
+, 0.30, -0.40, 0.30, 4.70, 0.30, 0.40, 0.30, 4.70
$
$ ---- Vertical strip body panel (XZ plane at y=0, normal +Y): 4 x 8 = 32 boxes
CAERO1, 500, 20, 0, 4, 8, 0, 0, 1
+, 0.30, 0.0, 0.05, 4.70, 0.30, 0.0, 0.45, 4.70
$
$ Body panels: SPLINE0 (zero structural coupling — negligible body elasticity).
$ Box-ID range = caero_eid + i_span*nchord + j_chord (horiz 16, vert 32 boxes).
SPLINE0, 9400, 400, 400, 415
SPLINE0, 9500, 500, 500, 531
$
ENDDATA
